From e1055cb89615458b55782a4f740892a5de99bf08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4pp4
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:43:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Add appindicator support for GTK 4

The GTK 4 client has no tray icon, because the appindicator libraries
need GTK 3. libayatana-appindicator-glib does not need GTK, but exports
the menu to org.gtk.Menus and org.gtk.Actions instead of
com.canonical.dbusmenu, and the Unity panel does not support them.

Implement the StatusNotifierItem interface and export the menu using
libdbusmenu-glib, which does not need GTK either. The existing
WITH_APPINDICATOR option enables it. The menu uses the actions that
add-global-menu-support.patch adds to the window.

gtkmm removes a hidden window from the application, so its actions and
the global menu do not work when the window is shown again. Keep the
window in the application. This needs gtkmm 4.22.

When Transmission starts minimized, remember that the window is hidden.
Otherwise the first click on Show Transmission does nothing.

https://github.com/transmission/transmission/issues/7364

Signed-off-by: c4pp4
